//! The Fourier coefficients of the geodesic integrals I1, I2 and I3 and of the reversion of I1, to
//! sixth order (Karney, "Algorithms for geodesics", J. Geodesy 87 (2013) 43-55, eqs. 15-25 and
//! 41-43). Generated by `derivations/ellipsoid_geodesic.mac`, which expands them from the integrands
//! and checks them against the elliptic integrals at 50 digits; do not edit by hand.
//! `derivations/verify.sh` regenerates this file and compares it byte for byte.
//!
//! Every coefficient is an exact rational `p / q`; each list is ascending in its variable.

/// `(1 - eps) A1`, in powers of `eps^2`.
#[rustfmt::skip]
pub(crate) const A1: [f64; 4] = [1.0, 1.0 / 4.0, 1.0 / 64.0, 1.0 / 256.0];

/// `C1_l = eps^l sum_j C1[l - 1][j] eps^(2 j)`, `l = 1..=6`.
